Q07 checkpoint and per-question recovery implementation validation
Date: 2026-09-27
Owner repository: StockQAbyLLM
Scope: additive SQLite checkpoint store + shared receipt hash + isolated regressions
Note: The initial snapshot below is retained as history. Its hashes, 234-test result, and pending-review note are superseded by the final exact-snapshot verification at the end of this file.

Command:
python -B -X utf8 -m pytest -q -o addopts='' -p no:cacheprovider -p no:base_url --basetemp=<unique TEMP/TMP child> tests/unit/test_quick_scan_work_store.py tests/unit/test_quick_scan_work_transport.py tests/unit/test_llm_client.py tests/unit/test_llm_provider.py tests/unit/test_search_provider.py tests/integration/test_quick_scan_cli.py

Result: 234 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped.
Static checks: Ruff passed; Black check passed; git diff --check passed.
Test isolation: pytest --basetemp, TMP and TEMP used a unique external temporary root; the root was removed and prior environment values restored. PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE was restored. One .pyc created by an earlier syntax probe was removed. No fixture, SQLite, WAL/SHM, coverage, or pytest cache output was retained in the StockQA repository.
External effects: no live API call, search-provider request, company-document download, or StockWiki/company-wiki write.

Covered behavior:
- SQLite schema v1 → v2 migration is additive and preserves work items, attempts, and event history; inconsistent v1 result_ready rows fail closed without migration.
- Checkpoint persistence binds the normalized score/status/description to exact entity/question and immutable identity/question/routing fingerprints, verified identity, successful completed search receipt, source URLs, response/model/provider IDs, and both durable-work and provider prompt hashes.
- The LLM HTTP transport's provider attempt ID is distinct from the work-store attempt ID; both are preserved. Receipt hashing is centralized and binds completion time and source URLs while excluding raw provider content.
- A checkpoint insert, work_item=result_ready transition, and work_event are atomic. An injected transition failure rolls the entire transaction back; identical replay is idempotent and changed answer replay conflicts; checkpoints cannot be updated/deleted and corrupt payload hashes fail closed.
- On restart, four checkpointed questions remain complete and only two pending questions can be claimed. response_available without a checkpoint remains leased and becomes uncertain after expiry; it is never silently skipped or reposted.
- Only pending work can be cancelled; cancellation is idempotent and a leased in-flight question remains leased.
- An end-to-end isolated test exercised the real LLMClient and ordered cascade, a fake HTTP response at the network boundary, strict response parsing, and a real temporary SQLite checkpoint.

